</tr>
<tr>
<td>Gradient</td>
<td>The vector of partial derivatives; points in the direction of steepest increase of the loss</td>
<td>Slope of the loss curve at the current weights</td>
<td>Understanding gradients lets you diagnose why training is stuck</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>Learning rate</td>
<td>The step-size multiplier on the negative gradient</td>
<td>η = 0.01 versus η = 1.0</td>
